  "name": "Saronen (Madurese shawm band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Outdoor shawm band of Madura, said to have originated in Sumenep and named after its lead instrument, the saronen, a conical wooden shawm (here the serunai card). The documented nine-piece band sets the saronen over a large gendang and a small gendang dik-gudik (here the generic membrane-drum card), three kenong, a kempul, a large gong and a korca, and it accompanies the kerapan sapi bull races and sapi sonok cattle contests as well as ritual ceremonies and processions.",
